[[File:Groom (Beta 32.1).png|thumb|218x218px|Beta 32.1]]
Groom's effect during its release in '''Beta 30.0''' allowed you to draw a card with a cost equal to your gold. '''Beta 32.1''' buffed that by now drawing a card with a cost equal to your remaining gold, so you can play the drawn card right away if you want. '''Beta 41.1''' buffed this further by now letting you draw a card with a cost less than your remaining gold if you lack one with equal cost, so the effect will now work almost all the time.
[[File:Groom (Beta 41.1).png|thumb|217x217px|Beta 41.1]]
'''Beta 48.0''' reworked it completely. Going from a 3/2/3, it's now a 4/4/4 (thus gaining +1G and +2/+1) and has a Turbo effect which simply lets you draw a card, but only if you have 6 or less in your hand (so you don't overdraw it instantly).

